# Live pipeline output. Regenerated from the raw corpus by the worker; never
# committed. data/seed/ below is the committed counterpart that ships in the
# deployed image -- see backend/citinel/web/app.py's source resolution.
data/incidents/
data/cache/enrichment/
!data/seed/
backend/uv.lock

# Swytchcode: the integration bundles (3.5 MB of vendor API definitions, no
# credentials -- scanned) are COMMITTED. They used to be ignored on the premise
# that `swy bootstrap` regenerates them on clone, but bootstrap requires a
# logged-in session and the Render container has none, so both ecosystem legs
# failed there with "bundle missing" before policy or credentials were ever
# consulted. Committing them makes the image deterministic and offline, which
# is what the kernel itself promises. Locks stay ignored.
.swytchcode/tooling.json.lock
.swytchcode/**/*.lock

.swytchcode/workspace.json

